Stripe’s Model Context Protocol (MCP) server supports two primary authentication methods: OAuth and restricted API keys [1][2]. OAuth is the recommended approach as it provides granular permissions and avoids sharing secret keys [1][2]. When using an MCP client that supports OAuth, the client will open a consent page to authorize access [1][2].

If your client does not support OAuth, you can authenticate using a restricted API key passed as a bearer token in the Authorization header [1][2].

Example configuration for a client:

```json
{
  "stripe": {
    "url": "https://mcp.stripe.com",
    "headers": {
      "Authorization": "Bearer <restricted_api_key>"
    }
  }
}
```

For connected accounts, pass the Stripe-Account header alongside your restricted API key [1].

The Klaviyo Model Context Protocol (MCP) server allows AI clients to interact with your Klaviyo data by acting as a wrapper for Klaviyo APIs [1][2]. To authenticate the MCP server, you can use either OAuth or a private API key depending on your setup [1][3].

For most MCP clients, you configure the server by providing a private API key in the environment variables of your configuration file [1][3]. Use the following structure for your configuration:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "klaviyo": {
      "command": "uvx",
      "args": ["klaviyo-mcp-server@latest"],
      "env": {
        "PRIVATE_API_KEY": "YOUR_API_KEY",
        "READ_ONLY": "false",
        "ALLOW_USER_GENERATED_CONTENT": "false"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Alternatively, when using custom connectors in platforms like Claude or ChatGPT, you can select OAuth authentication and follow the prompted authorization flow to grant the AI access to your account [1][3]. Ensure you have an Owner, Admin, or Manager role to manage these credentials [1][4][2].

To authenticate with the monday.com Model Context Protocol (MCP) server, you can use a personal API token or OAuth 2.0 [1].

For personal use, prototyping, or testing, use a personal API token [2]. Retrieve it by navigating to your profile picture, selecting Developers, and clicking My access tokens [2]. Pass this token in the Authorization header as a Bearer token [2]:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "monday-mcp": {
      "url": "https://mcp.monday.com/mcp",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer YOUR_API_TOKEN"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

For organizational control or public integrations, use an OAuth app to manage scopes and user access [3][4].
